{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571861-representing-attribute-changes","id":571861,"title":"Representing Attribute Changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-28T14:08:31-07:00","id":571861,"title":"Representing Attribute Changes","content":"In life you were a stylish debater and a master of social conflict. However you've realized that existence among the undead is a little more dangerous, so you decide to learn how to fight. You get some training with weapons and put some dots into Weaponry and then your player decides he wants to increase your Strength.<br /> <br /> How is this represented in game? Does the Vampire start hitting the gym every night? Furthermore, since your physical appearance gets &quot;frozen&quot; at the time of embrace how does this interact with a kindred who buffs up? Could you have a Vampire who was embraced as a weak skinny guy but is now incredibly buff (but still looks the same)?<br /> <br /> How do you handle this in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:19:43-07:00","id":571887,"title":"","content":"I think vampire strength is more mystical than physical. A vampire will look as strong as they were at embrace even when they can pick up a car. <br /> <br /> As such, strength training is probably not quite the same for a vamp. I would suggest rather than lifting weights you might need to use physical intensity repeatedly to get your body used to pushing power through your muscles until it can do it naturally without using up vitae. Or perhaps apply the principles gained from learning vigor. I mean, it's either the same price or less per dot as strength and comes with some side benefits, so it makes sense that vampires would usually max it out before turning on the attribute itself. Same for resilience and stamina, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:37:21-07:00","id":571898,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the pale skinny dude picking up a dumpster and smashing you with it is pretty thematic for vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T16:58:08-07:00","id":572007,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with what's already been said, but it might be useful to distinguish the <i>experience</i> of growing in power through supernatural Vigor from simply increasing in raw strength. While Vampires are mostly static, they do change in certain ways over time; the most obvious example is that vampires start looking more &quot;dead&quot; as their humanity decreases, which may be a useful starting point. Maybe a vampire whose strength increases doesn't look any different on the surface, but when others touch him his muscles feel <i>harder</i>, like the stiff sinews of a mummified corpse. Likewise, increasing stamina might give his skin the tactile quality of cured leather, even as he remains unchanged to most senses.<br /> <br /> These changes might manifest as an adaptation to a rougher lifestyle; the process could be roughly analogous to the benefits of regular exercise, but would be driven by the same supernatural forces that give the Vampire's body mobility to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-28-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:50:50-07:00","id":573299,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's kind of a limit on the whole &quot;skinny vamp chucks a truck&quot; phenomenon. A person who is taking the time to enhance natural strength should be gaining muscle mass, even if the muscle mass is being fueled by supernatural blood syrup instead of oxygen and sugar. And as for Physical Intensity, I always imagine a sudden jump in strength to look like Bane getting pumped full of Venom: You're &quot;metabolizing&quot; (in the loosest sense of the word) Vitae to quickly produce short-lived muscle mass, create artificial &quot;super-adrenaline&quot;, or toughen your skin and flesh.<br /> <br /> But again, in your own games, you can choose to make it all &quot;Muscles Are Meaningless&quot; type strength if you want, and it's a totally valid interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:05:49-07:00","id":573305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571861-representing-attribute-changes?p=573299#post573299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's kind of a limit on the whole &quot;skinny vamp chucks a truck&quot; phenomenon. A person who is taking the time to enhance natural strength should be gaining muscle mass, even if the muscle mass is being fueled by supernatural blood syrup instead of oxygen and sugar. And as for Physical Intensity, I always imagine a sudden jump in strength to look like Bane getting pumped full of Venom: You're &quot;metabolizing&quot; (in the loosest sense of the word) Vitae to quickly produce short-lived muscle mass, create artificial &quot;super-adrenaline&quot;, or toughen your skin and flesh.<br /> <br /> But again, in your own games, you can choose to make it all &quot;Muscles Are Meaningless&quot; type strength if you want, and it's a totally valid interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a reasonable way to run it, for sure. With permanent physical changes only costing a point of Willpower now instead of a dot, it'd be pretty easy to say the character spends all night pumping iron and then spends a willpower before he goes to bed each morning, so his increased muscle mass will &quot;stick.&quot; Hey, maybe your personal trainer is your Touchstone, so you gain the Willpower back when you interact with him each night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:43:30-07:00","id":573313,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like that idea a lot. You don't necessarily <i>need </i>to build up real muscle mass to get stronger, but if you do it is indeed functional. <br /> <br /> I would include a caveat that you can only ever get to human maximum in this manner though. To get past 5 at high BP you need to embrace your undeadness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T17:19:01-07:00","id":573335,"title":"","content":"A vampire with a bodybuilder's forum as his touchstone. But oh no! The InBoard has discovered his selfies plastered all over their VIP section!<br /> <br /> An idea that occurred to me to help explain why you'll sometimes see Elders with higher Attributes than the mortal maximum: What if every dot of Blood Potency you gain becomes a 1 XP discount on your next Attribute purchase, down to a minimum of 1 Experience, and it resets everytime you purchase a new dot? That's an unnecessary little rules thing, but if anyone ever plays a generational game, could be a fun way for characters to accumulate those cool superhuman stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:32:57-07:00","id":573428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571861-representing-attribute-changes?p=572007#post572007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree with what's already been said, but it might be useful to distinguish the <i>experience</i> of growing in power through supernatural Vigor from simply increasing in raw strength. While Vampires are mostly static, they do change in certain ways over time; the most obvious example is that vampires start looking more &quot;dead&quot; as their humanity decreases, which may be a useful starting point. Maybe a vampire whose strength increases doesn't look any different on the surface, but when others touch him his muscles feel <i>harder</i>, like the stiff sinews of a mummified corpse. Likewise, increasing stamina might give his skin the tactile quality of cured leather, even as he remains unchanged to most senses.<br /> <br /> These changes might manifest as an adaptation to a rougher lifestyle; the process could be roughly analogous to the benefits of regular exercise, but would be driven by the same supernatural forces that give the Vampire's body mobility to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this interpretation, and it's definitely how I'd describe an Elder with high attributes. I'd imagine this process takes decades or more though, so if a Neonate wants to buff up quickly (and for some reason Vigor isn't an option) or simply wants to change their appearance there should be other avenues to do it. Perhaps the Ordo Dracul provide a treatment where they administer a mix of chemicals, electrical shocks and blood to trick your dead flesh into thinking it's alive. Vampires availing of this service can benefit from exercise the same way a mortal can (though obviously the Dragons don't provide this for free).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:23:40-07:00","id":573771,"title":"","content":"The way I run things is that your regular attributes reflect a change to your physical body. We're not looking at creatures of pure stasis like Masquerade anymore - changes do happen to a vampire's body over time, and you do deviate from the moment of your Embrace. Especially at low BP and high Humanity. If you want the pale, skinny guy lifting a dumpster, that's where Vigor, bonuses from frenzy, and blood buffing comes in.<br /> <br /> So, in my mind, a vampire who's putting in the effort to exercise will gain muscle mass and tone. If its an attribute, skill, or non-supernatural merit, then any physical changes that would happen to a mortal, I have happen to the vampire as well. If its a supernatural effect, then ignore it.<br /> <br /> It might not be the most popular way of looking at it, but its how I see things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:45:10-07:00","id":573821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571861-representing-attribute-changes?p=573771#post573771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TWe're not looking at creatures of pure stasis like Masquerade anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>do </i>however revert to their embrace appearance every time the sleep. I'm not sure how gaining muscle mass the normal way could be the default here. <br /> <br /> Also I can think of a few examples where that would just look <i>wrong.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:09:46-07:00","id":573854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571861-representing-attribute-changes?p=573821#post573821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>do </i>however revert to their embrace appearance every time the sleep. I'm not sure how gaining muscle mass the normal way could be the default here.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) Unless effort is expanded to keep the changes. And having a dedicated workout is an effort of will.<br /> <br /> 2) Mutation of the blood happen.<br /> <br /> 3) Buying Striking Looks can represent a change in appearance, so there's precedent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I can think of a few examples where that would just look <i>wrong.</i> </div> </div> </div> I can think of a few examples where it'd look wrong with regular mortals as well. That'll happen anytime you try to turn humans into just numbers. Unless you have something specific in mind you want to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-30-2015, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:19:55-07:00","id":573856,"title":"","content":"Also, I specifically said that it was how I saw things; you want to do it another way, then do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T07:04:39-07:00","id":573903,"title":"","content":"This is an old argument for me (or at least an old topic). I don't see the Attributes as stark representations based on the words used to describe them. To me, &quot;Strength&quot; is not just &quot;muscle mass&quot; and Intelligence is not &quot;how smart you are&quot; and Composure isn't necessarily how &quot;in control of your reactions&quot; you are. To me, what you really have to look at is the cross between the two <i>types</i> of Attributes:<br /> <br /> On the one hand, you have the columns: Mental. Physical. Social.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you have the rows: Power. Finesse. Resistance.<br /> <br /> Your Intelligence isn't necessarily how smart you are; you could have high Wits and be super snappy and a quick-thinker who comes up with brilliant plants, while having low intelligence. Intelligence is your ability to impose your Mental self on the world. It is your Mental Power. It is your Mental Strength. It is your Mental Presence.<br /> <br /> At the same time, your Strength isn't necessarily how <i>strong</i> you are, but <i>how efficiently you use your body to impose yourself on the world</i>. Where as Stamina isn't necessarily how tough you are but rather <i>how efficiently you resist the things other and the world physically impose on you</i>. Finesse Attributes are about subtlety and avoidance, and strike a sort of balance between the two.<br /> <br /> This interpretation also has the advantage of shutting down people who can't wrap their heads around a small or thin person with Strength 5. Yes, they should probably have more muscle mass, but at least this way we can reliably accept, via suspension of disbelief, the infamous Waif Fu trope, among others.<br /> <br /> And this applies the same way to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:46:17-07:00","id":578404,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of those interpretations are wrong. I think that closing yourself on one interpretation, only, is wrong. I usually handle this in a simple way: I ask the player how HIS character do this.<br /> <br /> Any reasonable answer will do. And reasonable means just that he trully envisioned the change being aplied to the character instead of it being a meaningless dot on the sheet. The actual meaning isn't as important as a meaning being present to start with. That's all.<br /> <br /> Real life already have the precedence. There ARE people that get most of their strength just by applying it best than most. There ARE people with more efficient muscles without huge muscle mass. And, of course, there are bodybuilders. We can't be so strict on reallity, why should we be on a game?<br /> <br /> But yes, V:tR already showed more than once that you CAN change phisically during undeath, it just do not follow living tissue logic anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}